Winterhalde Estate description = {The mage family Winterhalde have had many estates, most of which are now currently run down. The following is a description of the one Nini has been sent to serve at the start of the story: a manor deep in the woods where the nights are darker and the moon somehow brighter. The estate is a study-retreat clearly made by and for a wizarding family. Nini found it a crumbling, ghost-haunted ruin, and one year into Nini's stewardship, it remains barely serviceable. She has kept the bedrooms, guest rooms, dining hall, and one of the workshops in good enough states, but the armory and alchemy lab are collapsed and will require skilled labor to repair. Nini has tended to the gardens well but the fountains don't work anymore. There is a library with general and light reading, whose books Nini has devoured. The manor interior has busts and paintings depicting the greats of the old Winterhalde family.

The manor has an entrance to a crystal cave which leads to the wider crystal cavern complexes of Agartha, the World Below. Agartha itself is its own magical world of golems, gnomes, and giant insects, but its connection to the manor seems to be haunted by powerful undead. The entrance is boarded up, shackled, and warded. Nini, in her capacity as a novice glamour mage, speculates that the wards may fail in about a year, and then wraiths will come from below and kill all the new inhabitants of the manor. This detail is not mentioned in the deed to the place.

The estate encompasses the manor itself and the surrounding dark woodland. The woodland is magically attuned to the spheres of astral and death, the latter more than the former. Sometimes undead animals will roam about as zombies before dying for real, but thankfully no cursed things more dangerous than ghouls and ghosts have been reported. The area may be considered dangerous to normal people.}
